WHAT IS DERIVED FROM WHAT
-------------------------

  profiles/machine/QIDI i-Fast 0.4 nozzle.json
      inherits  Qidi X-Max 0.4 nozzle
        -> fdm_qidi_common -> fdm_machine_common
      from OrcaSlicer v2.4.2, Qidi vendor bundle 02.04.00.06
      (resources/profiles/Qidi/machine/ in the OrcaSlicer source tree)

  profiles/process/*.json
      inherit   0.12mm Fine / 0.16mm Optimal / 0.20mm Standard /
                0.25mm Draft / 0.30mm Extra Draft @Qidi XMax
        -> fdm_process_qidi_common -> fdm_process_common
      same bundle

  profiles/filament/QIDI Generic PLA @QIDI i-Fast.json
      inherits  Qidi Generic PLA
        -> fdm_filament_pla -> fdm_filament_common
      same bundle

Values that do NOT come from that chain come from one of two QIDI sources, both
of which are QIDI Technology's own published output for this machine and are
reproduced here unmodified as reference material, not as part of the profile:

  reference/qidi-profiles/    QIDI's published legacy profile bundle
                              (PrusaSlicer / Cura / Simplify3D / ideaMaker)
  reference/*.gcode           G-code exported by QIDI Print for the i-Fast

Both directories are read-only inputs. See README.md for which value came from
which source, and TODO.md for the values that are still unverified.

